<!--BlockML Transformer — README
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.transformer.README-->
<transformer:README xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:transformer="org.blockml.bml.transformer"
  xmlns:transformercap="org.blockml.bml.transformer.capability"
  xmlns:transformerdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.transformer.documentation"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow">

  <baseType>
    core:ReadMe
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Reading entry for the Transformer library
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The @blockml/transformer package owns the BlockML transformer library
    (org.blockml.bml.transformer.*). Workflow types live in
    org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow.*. Process steps live in
    org.blockml.bml.transformer.capability.*.
    
    The TypeScript engine executes ModelTransformation instances via
    `blockml transform apply EXECUTION-FQN [--library path] [--parameters JSON] [--parameter-mappings JSON]`.
    `--library` selects the target Library.bml for `_meta`; omitted uses
    cwd `package.json` `blockml.library`. Apply sources are
    `_meta.transform.pending` (`template=false`, relocated),
    `_meta.transform.available` (`template=true`, copied), or a template
    outside `_meta.transform`. Transformer.run prepares the
    execution, then runs each concrete `workflow:ModelOperation` in
    order: persist operation Running, dispatch the registered
    OperationExecutor, Reflect, Persist results onto that operation,
    commit. Default Prepare and Finalize are deterministic. Default
    executor for AgenticOperation is AgenticExecutor (isolated agent;
    changes BML model source only, not ModelTransformation /
    `_meta/transform/`). Default executor for ToolOperation is
    ToolExecutor (npm CLI via npx). Default Reflect is deterministic: git
    `changedFiles` after the executor, and `output` when the
    operation's `captureOutput` is true. Default Persist writes those
    fields onto the ModelOperation that just ran. When that operation
    succeeds, Persist applies its `resultMappings` onto `result`. A
    mapping fault writes ResultException onto the operation, fails it,
    and aborts remaining operations.     After a started execution, Finalize
    relocates the Block to `_meta.transform.succeeded` only when every
    ModelOperation succeeded, otherwise `_meta.transform.failed`.
    Finalize writes `duration` (wall-clock elapsed from Prepare
    through Finalize) and the complete lifecycle line prints
    `Elapsed …`.     Prepare
    `parameterMappings` faults fill `exception` with ParametersException
    and skip operations. A ModelOperation failure leaves
    `ModelTransformation.exception` empty and aborts remaining
    operations. Prepare requires a clean Git
    worktree (nearest enclosing toplevel from cwd; cwd may be a
    package directory), records `baseCommit`, and commits the running relocation.
    Each ModelOperation commits Running first (recovery boundary), then
    commits model changes together with the operation terminal state.
    Finalize commits the terminal relocation. Transformation intelligence
    lives in the model, not in the engine.
  </documentation>
